{"id":"the-synchronous-recipe","name":"The synchronous recipe","chapter":"Four handed siteswaps","kind":"guide","page":36,"label":"35","jugglers":2,"objects":null,"timing":"sync","pdf":"https://www.jugglingedge.com/pdf/highgate.pdf#page=36&view=FitH,779","passist":null,"notations":[{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"(6x,6x)(8,6)(8x,8x)(2,8)(6,2)"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"(2x,2x)(4,2)(4x,4x)"}],"derived":null,"body":[{"t":"li","h":"Take any synchronous siteswap. I&#x27;m going to choose (6x,6x)(8,6)(8x,8x)(2,8)(6,2), which is"},{"t":"p","h":"a six object pattern."},{"t":"li","h":"Subtract 4 from every number to give a derived siteswap. In my example the derived"},{"t":"p","h":"siteswap is (2x,2x)(4,2)(4x,4x)(-2,4)(2,-2)."},{"t":"li","h":"The first number in each bracket is Anne&#x27;s throw, the second number is Ben&#x27;s throw."},{"t":"li","h":"An x after a number shows a pass."},{"t":"li","h":"Number the beats in a causal diagram as follows:"},{"t":"d","i":0},{"t":"li","h":"Note that both jugglers throw at the same time on odd numbered beats and no-one throws"},{"t":"p","h":"on even numbered beats!"},{"t":"li","h":"For Anne&#x27;s throw on beat 1, add the first number in the derived siteswap: 2, you get 1+2=3."},{"t":"p","h":"The first 2 is followed by an x, so on the digram draw a line from Anne&#x27;s beat 1 to Ben&#x27;s beat 3:"},{"t":"d","i":1},{"t":"li","h":"For Ben&#x27;s throw on beat 1, add the second number in the derived siteswap: 2, you get"},{"t":"p","h":"1+2=3. This 2 is followed by an x, so on the digram draw a line from Ben&#x27;s beat 1 to Anne&#x27;s beat 3:"},{"t":"d","i":2},{"t":"li","h":"For Anne&#x27;s throw on beat 3, add the third number in the derived siteswap: 4, you get 3+4=7."},{"t":"p","h":"So on the digram draw a line from Anne&#x27;s beat 3 to her beat 7:"},{"t":"d","i":3},{"t":"li","h":"For Ben&#x27;s throw on beat 3, add the fourth number in the derived siteswap: 2, you get"},{"t":"p","h":"3+2=5. So on the digram draw a line from Ben&#x27;s beat 3 to his beat 5:"},{"t":"d","i":4},{"t":"li","h":"For Anne&#x27;s throw on beat 5, add the fifth number in the derived siteswap: 4, you get 5+4=9."},{"t":"p","h":"This 4 is followed by an x, so on the digram draw a line from Anne&#x27;s beat 4 to Ben&#x27;s beat 9:"},{"t":"d","i":5},{"t":"li","h":"For Ben&#x27;s throw on beat 5, add the sixth number in the derived siteswap: 4, you get 5+4=9."},{"t":"p","h":"This 4 is followed by an x, so on the digram draw a line from Ben&#x27;s beat 4 to Anne&#x27;s beat 9:"},{"t":"d","i":6},{"t":"li","h":"For Anne&#x27;s throw on beat 7, add the seventh number in the derived siteswap: -2, you get"},{"t":"p","h":"7-2=5. So on the digram draw a line from Anne&#x27;s beat 7 to her beat 5:"},{"t":"d","i":7},{"t":"li","h":"For Ben&#x27;s throw on beat 7, add the eighth number in the derived siteswap: 4, you get"},{"t":"p","h":"7+4=11. So on the digram draw a line from Ben&#x27;s beat 7 to his beat 11:"},{"t":"d","i":8},{"t":"li","h":"For Anne&#x27;s throw on beat 9, add the ninth number in the derived siteswap: 2, you get"},{"t":"p","h":"9+2=11. So on the digram draw a line from Anne&#x27;s beat 9 to her beat 11:"},{"t":"d","i":9},{"t":"li","h":"For Ben&#x27;s throw on beat 9, add the tenth number in the derived siteswap: -2, you get 9-2=7."},{"t":"p","h":"So on the digram draw a line from Ben&#x27;s beat 9 to his beat 7:"},{"t":"d","i":10},{"t":"li","h":"As there is no eleventh or twelfth number in the derived siteswap, to work out the next"},{"t":"p","h":"throws for both jugglers we return to the beginning of the derived siteswap."},{"t":"li","h":"If you apply the same procedure for all the remaining beats you end up with the following"},{"t":"p","h":"pattern:"},{"t":"d","i":11},{"t":"p","h":"Both jugglers start with two clubs in their right hand and one club in their left hand. Anne&#x27;s pattern is: pass heff double zip self. This pattern is called not why. Ben&#x27;s pattern is: pass self double heff zip. This pattern is called why not? Both jugglers throw straight single passes and crossing doubles."},{"t":"p","h":"Note that both jugglers could pass not why or why not? I chose the combined pattern to distinguish between Anne&#x27;s and Ben&#x27;s passes more easily."},{"t":"p","h":"There is another way to juggle this pattern as a four handed siteswap. Both jugglers can throw crossing single passes and straight doubles."},{"t":"d","i":12},{"t":"p","h":"Ben starts with two clubs in his left hand and one in his right hand and his first throw is left handed. This pattern is a bit collision prone, but there are other patterns where it&#x27;s better if both jugglers throw crossing single passes and straight doubles!"}],"drawings":[{"file":"p36-1.png","kind":"causal diagram","reading":{"rows":[{"juggler":"A","name":"Anne","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R","n":1},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L","n":3},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R","n":5},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L","n":7},{"t":4.0,"hand":"R","n":9},{"t":5.0,"hand":"L","n":11},{"t":6.0,"hand":"R","n":13},{"t":7.0,"hand":"L","n":15},{"t":8.0,"hand":"R","n":17},{"t":9.0,"hand":"L","n":19},{"t":10.0,"hand":"R","n":21}]},{"juggler":"B","name":"Ben","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":4.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":5.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":6.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":7.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":8.0,"hand":"R"},{"t":9.0,"hand":"L"},{"t":10.0,"hand":"R"}]}],"arrows":[],"holds":"unlinked","sync":false,"grid":2,"unit_px":63.0,"layout":{"x0":132.0,"unit":63.0,"rows_y":[48.0,111.0],"names":[[10,30,99,59,"Anne"],[35,93,99,121,"Ben"]],"dots":[]},"labels":[{"row":1,"t":0.5,"n":2,"below":true},{"row":1,"t":1.5,"n":4,"below":true},{"row":1,"t":2.5,"n":6,"below":true},{"row":1,"t":3.5,"n":8,"below":true},{"row":1,"t":4.5,"n":10,"below":true},{"row":1,"t":5.5,"n":12,"below":true},{"row":1,"t":6.5,"n":14,"below":true},{"row":1,"t":7.5,"n":16,"below":true},{"row":1,"t":8.5,"n":18,"below